    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "eyebrow": "01 · The thesis",
      "title": "The technology is not the story. The cost line is.",
      "body": "Staples are a volume business with thin margins and powerful distribution. Technology matters when it changes input cost, waste or shelf productivity. The biggest long-run shifts are biological production of ingredients, AI-driven forecasting, and retail media turning shelf space into an advertising business."
    },
    {
      "kind": "points",
      "eyebrow": "02 · Sector economics",
      "title": "What this sector actually sells",
      "body": "Revenue grows slowly with population and price. Gross margin depends on commodity inputs, packaging and manufacturing efficiency; distribution and trade spend absorb much of the rest.",
      "bullets": [
        "Volume growth is low; price/mix and market share drive reported growth.",
        "Commodity inputs swing gross margin, often with a lag to pricing.",
        "Trade promotion and shelf space are the main competitive currencies.",
        "Distribution density determines cost per case.",
        "Retail media and private label are reshaping retailer economics."
      ]
    },
